    <statement><p>Find <m>dy/dx</m> in terms of <m>x</m> and <m>y</m> 
if
<m>\cos^2(6 y) + \sin^2(6 y) = y + 3</m>.</p>
<p><m>{dy\over dx} =</m> <fillin characters="65" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>\cos^2\theta+\sin^2\theta=1</m>, the equation becomes:
<m>1=y+3</m> or <m>y=-2</m>. Hence, <m>\frac{dy}{dx}=0</m>.



</solution>
